# Captured from dm.exe 516.1687, not hand-written.
#
# Each row is a path whose final segment names a member the SPELLING cannot reach:
#   /obj/lever/pull  declared `verb/pull()`, so only /obj/lever/verb/pull reaches it
#   /obj/crate/hp    a var, which never satisfies a path's final segment
#   /obj/crate/proc  the container, on a type that declares no proc of its own
#
#   /obj/winch/verb/haul   the right name through the WRONG marker: haul is a proc
#   .proc/nope_xyz   the RELATIVE spelling, with no anchor up the enclosing type's path
#                    ancestors declaring it
#
# `total` pins the controls' silence, which is the half that matters here: a bare override
# reachable without a marker, the marker form itself, a container on a type that has procs,
# the nameof() form that resolves through inheritance where the plain expression does not,
# and the two relative forms that reach the enclosing type and a path ancestor.
#
# "return/obj/lever/pull" is the source's "return /obj/lever/pull" — dm.exe strips whitespace
# when it echoes the offending text, so these rows match on a substring.
65 error /obj/lever/pull: undefined type path
72 error /obj/crate/hp: undefined type path
76 error /obj/crate/proc: undefined type path
85 error /obj/winch/verb/haul: undefined type path
107 error .proc/nope_xyz: undefined type path
